      "value": "@{5ce3b1457bebcb66c29b850d|full_name}: Do you mean DDoS? In that case, it is nearly unavoidable, as all they have to do is grab your IP, then go to a site like internetstresstest and send millions of packets your way, almost untrackable. However, that is what you get for a free game, and a paid VPN such as WTFast can decrease latency (as if that would do anything on VRChat) but hide your IP at the same time. Because of how big the servers there are, overloading is impossible.\nThere are less fortunate people on VRChat who messed up miserably in real life, and those issues bleeding into VRChat, entitling others to permanently DDoS their IP anytime he joins VRChat, even after he has lost connection.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
